@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+Zahir Uddin is an enterprise technology executive with more than 25 years of experience leading ERP, HRIS, and finance-adjacent platform strategy across life sciences and other regulated industries. Most recently, he served as Head of IT at SK Life Science, Inc. in Paramus, NJ, where he owned the enterprise application ecosystem supporting $1B in annual commercial operations, reduced technology operating expenses by 30% through vendor renegotiation, cloud rightsizing, and license consolidation, and built a pragmatic data governance framework anchored by a COO-chaired governance council spanning Finance, Legal, HR, IT, and QA. Under his leadership, the organization's Snowflake and Power BI analytics platform grew to roughly 150 production dashboards serving approximately 400 business users across Commercial, Finance, Supply Chain, and HR.
+
+Earlier at SK Life Science, as Head of Applications and previously Enterprise Architect, Zahir led the enterprise systems work behind the company's first U.S. pharmaceutical product launch, delivering a validated application ecosystem within fourteen months and modernizing identity infrastructure to cut licensing costs by 58%. He has directed AI-enabled automation initiatives spanning security operations, predictive analytics for field engagement, and expense anomaly detection, and has partnered directly with HR, Finance, Legal, and Supply Chain leaders on ERP, HRIS, and compliance-driven platform strategy under SOX and GxP frameworks.
+
+Before SK Life Science, he held consulting and delivery leadership roles at Streebo, Reltio, Univision, and Project Performance Corporation, building master data management and enterprise data warehouse programs for pharmaceutical and consumer clients. He holds a Bachelor of Science in Information Systems from Brunel University London and is an Oracle Certified Professional.